  "body": "## Privacy\n\n- **Quiet telemetry**: Fire OS won't let its reporting apps be disabled (device and app metrics, crash reports, app-usage statistics, ad links, remote support, ceviche, remote diagnostics). *Quiet* takes \"run in the background\" from all eight and app-usage access from the statistics proxy; *Let them run* puts them back. Journaled, so Restore defaults and Undo everything cover it.\n- **Location** on/off switch (the stick ships with location on \"high accuracy\").\n- **Limit ads & tracking** now also sets Amazon's device-usage-data, app-usage-data and marketing-metrics switches.\n- The \"Right now\" card shows all four states, and the DNS card says which preset blocks which Amazon hosts (AdGuard: the metrics hosts; NextDNS with its Amazon list: those plus the event and impression hosts used by Amazon's built-in reporting services).\n\n## Small things\n\n- The Speed page's \"Wake an app…\" list no longer shows the quieted reporting apps as apps you put to sleep.\n\nInstall: open the APK below with Downloader (`https://github.com/MohamedNofal/stickman/releases/latest/download/stickman.apk`). Upgrading keeps your settings.\n"
